 ## Background
-SA-GS was introduced in the paper "SA-GS: Semantic-Aware Gaussian Splatting for Large Scene Reconstruction with Geometry Constrain" [S1, unofficial]. It extends previous work like LangSplat and LeGaussian, which use large vision models for object-level semantics, by applying semantic and geometric data to large-scale scenes [S1, unofficial]. It addresses the issue of uniform Gaussian distribution by adapting shapes to local geometric complexity.
